{"page":854,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.04911,"w":0.25475,"h":0.01851,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"840 Chapter 14: Partial Derivatives"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09051,"w":0.59301,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"To find an equation for the plane tangent to a smooth surface z = ƒ(x, y) at a point"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.10586,"w":0.59297,"h":0.04792,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"P0(x0, y0, z0) where z0 = ƒ(x0, y0), we first observe that the equation z = ƒ(x, y) is equiva- lent to ƒ(x, y) - z = 0. The surface z = ƒ(x, y) is therefore the zero level surface of the function F(x, y, z) = ƒ(x, y) - z. The partial derivatives of F are"},{"x":0.49592,"y":0.16517,"w":0.04788,"h":0.02698,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Fx = 0"},{"x":0.53399,"y":0.17236,"w":0.20096,"h":0.02386,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0x (ƒ(x, y) - z) = fx - 0 = fx"},{"x":0.49591,"y":0.1997,"w":0.04789,"h":0.02698,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Fy = 0"},{"x":0.53399,"y":0.20689,"w":0.20096,"h":0.02386,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0y (ƒ(x, y) - z) = fy - 0 = fy"},{"x":0.49591,"y":0.23678,"w":0.04684,"h":0.02698,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Fz = 0"},{"x":0.53336,"y":0.24398,"w":0.21704,"h":0.02386,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0z (ƒ(x, y) - z) = 0 - 1 = -1."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.2753,"w":0.08132,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The formula"},{"x":0.43842,"y":0.2977,"w":0.35875,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Fx(P0)(x - x0) + Fy(P0)( y - y0) + Fz(P0)(z - z0) = 0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.32646,"w":0.4314,"h":0.01594,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"for the plane tangent to the level surface at P0 therefore reduces to"},{"x":0.43461,"y":0.34885,"w":0.36636,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ƒx(x0, y0)(x - x0) + ƒy(x0, y0)( y - y0) - (z - z0) = 0."},{"x":0.35358,"y":0.41349,"w":0.53249,"h":0.05176,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Plane Tangent to a Surface z = ƒ(x, y) at (x0 , y0 , ƒ(x0 , y0)) The plane tangent to the surface z = ƒ(x, y) of a differentiable function ƒ at the point P0(x0, y0, z0) = (x0, y0, ƒ(x0, y0)) is"},{"x":0.35358,"y":0.47871,"w":0.5284,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"ƒx(x0, y0)(x - x0) + ƒy(x0, y0)( y - y0) - (z - z0) = 0.\b (3)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.5379,"w":0.57056,"h":0.01878,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Example 2 Find the plane tangent to the surface z = x cos y - yex at (0, 0, 0)."},{"x":0.22064,"y":0.56044,"w":0.07551,"h":0.02393,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"The plane x + z − 4 = 0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.56976,"w":0.59302,"h":0.03063,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Solution We calculate the partial derivatives of ƒ(x, y) = x cos y - yex and use Equation (3):"},{"x":0.22325,"y":0.58764,"w":0.04506,"h":0.01142,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"g(x, y, z)"},{"x":0.45828,"y":0.59798,"w":0.31133,"h":0.04822,"fs":0.01918,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"ƒx(0, 0) = (cos y - yex)(0,0) = 1 - 0 # 1 = 1 ƒy(0, 0) = (-x sin y - ex)(0,0) = 0 - 1 = -1."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.6539,"w":0.19534,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The tangent plane is therefore"},{"x":0.44681,"y":0.66659,"w":0.34276,"h":0.02949,"fs":0.0243,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"1 # (x - 0) - 1 # (y - 0) - (z - 0) = 0, Eq. (3)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.69994,"w":0.01363,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"or"},{"x":0.17262,"y":0.70351,"w":0.01449,"h":0.01149,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"∇g"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.72234,"w":0.35266,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"x - y - z = 0.\b"},{"x":0.22991,"y":0.72533,"w":0.06906,"h":0.01142,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"The ellipse E"},{"x":0.23563,"y":0.74159,"w":0.04143,"h":0.01142,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(1, 1, 3)"},{"x":0.20571,"y":0.75906,"w":0.01368,"h":0.01149,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"∇f"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.76042,"w":0.04613,"h":0.01164,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"∇f × ∇g"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.77901,"w":0.20438,"h":0.01687,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Example 3 The surfaces"},{"x":0.47627,"y":0.80154,"w":0.3316,"h":0.02712,"fs":0.0243,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ƒ(x, y, z) = x2 + y2 - 2 = 0 A cylinder"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.84257,"w":0.02362,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"and"},{"x":0.16403,"y":0.85323,"w":0.08359,"h":0.02392,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"The cylinder x2 + y2 − 2 = 0"},{"x":0.48855,"y":0.86293,"w":0.30505,"h":0.02712,"fs":0.0243,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"g(x, y, z) = x + z - 4 = 0 A plane"},{"x":0.17354,"y":0.8837,"w":0.04215,"h":0.01142,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"f(x, y, z)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.90396,"w":0.593,"h":0.03129,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"meet in an ellipse E (Figure 14.35). Find parametric equations for the line tangent to E at the point P0(1, 1, 3)."},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.90459,"w":0.25434,"h":0.0291,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Figure 14.35 This cylinder and plane intersect in an ellipse E (Example 3)."}]}